Show which profile is playing: a line in the main menu footer and a short message when EmulationStation starts.

Nothing is added when profiles are not in use (no named profile exists and the default one is active), so single-user setups see
nothing new.  The name comes from GuiProfilesSettings::getActiveProfileLabel(), which reads the same files as the profile screen
(display_name, then the RetroAchievements username, then the folder name).  A profile switch does not restart EmulationStation, so the
menu footer (built each time the menu opens) is where a change shows first.

